{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level data variable `y`, which appears exactly once on the left side of a built-in `normal` likelihood. All parameters have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before they are used in the model likelihood, and the remaining data variables are context inputs used only as sizes, indices, or predictors.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_airport;
  int<lower=0> n_treatment;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_airport> airport;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_treatment> treatment;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_airport] d;
  vector[n_treatment] g;
  real mu;
  real mu_d;
  real mu_g;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_d;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_g;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[n_airport] d_adj;
  vector[n_treatment] g_adj;
  real mu_adj;
  real mu_d2;
  real mu_g2;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  mu_g2 = mean(g);
  mu_d2 = mean(d);
  g_adj = g - mu_g2;
  d_adj = d - mu_d2;
  mu_adj = mu + mu_g2 + mu_d2;
  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = mu + g[treatment[i]] + d[airport[i]];
  }
}
model {
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_d ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_g ~ uniform(0, 100);
  mu ~ normal(0, 100);
  mu_g ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_d ~ normal(0, 1);
  g ~ normal(100 * mu_g, sigma_g);
  d ~ normal(100 * mu_d, sigma_d);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"airport":[3,2,3],"n_airport":3,"n_treatment":3,"treatment":[1,2,1],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
